  "name": "QuPath",
  "alternateName": [
    "Quantitative Pathology & Bioimage Analysis"
  ],
  "description": "Open-source desktop platform for digital pathology image analysis and bioimage informatics. Provides whole slide image (WSI) viewing, interactive cell detection and classification, tissue segmentation, TMA (tissue microarray) analysis, fluorescence image analysis, and a Groovy scripting interface for automating and extending workflows. Supports OpenSlide-compatible formats (SVS, NDPI, SCN, MRXS, OME-TIFF, and others). Machine learning classifiers can be trained interactively on annotated regions without leaving the application. Integrates with MONAI Label for AI-assisted annotation. GPL-3.0, 1.4k stars, v0.7.0 (March 2026). Published in Scientific Reports 2017 (DOI: 10.1038/s41598-017-17204-5) with 8,480+ citations — the most widely cited open-source digital pathology software. Developed by Peter Bankhead at the University of Edinburgh.",
