  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The de facto open-source platform for digital pathology — 8,480+ citations on the 2017 Scientific Reports paper make it the most widely cited pathology analysis software in existence. GPL-3.0, 1.4k stars, v0.7.0 March 2026 showing active maintenance. Supports WSI annotation, interactive cell classification, TMA analysis, and Groovy scripting for reproducible pipelines. Integrates natively with MONAI Label for AI-assisted annotation. Adopt for any team doing computational pathology, biomarker quantification, or training pathology AI models.",
